From d7d24f23bea40cb6e535914605a812b8d0e5b660 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wieslaw Soltes <wieslawsoltes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 12:43:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Fix Reveal border light position expression lifetime

RevealBorderLight creates its Offset expression as a temporary. Animation
snapshots hold live reference parameters weakly, so dropping the expression
also drops the pointer-position and SpotlightHeight property sets. After
the release batch, Offset evaluates to (0, 0, 0) and nearby Reveal borders
do not catch the pointer light.

Retain the expression in BorderResources for the connected spotlight's
lifetime, as RevealHoverLight already does. Disconnect and material-policy
resource replacement release it with the rest of the resources.

Add compositor regressions checking pointer movement for all four border
lights (normal/wide, light/dark themes), including material-policy resource
recreation. Both regressions fail before the fix with a zero Offset.

Validation: all seven media::media_tests tests pass with the fix.
---
 src/FerroUI.Controls/media/media_tests.rs   | 70 +++++++++++++++++++++
 src/FerroUI.Controls/media/reveal_lights.rs | 12 +++-
 2 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/FerroUI.Controls/media/media_tests.rs b/src/FerroUI.Controls/media/media_tests.rs
