From a22094a4c487ee1b43d62e21e41b998c0f2176f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wieslaw Soltes <wieslawsoltes@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 13:20:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Fix composition light discovery across rendering threads

Native rendering can alternate between synchronous UI-thread frames and
render-thread frames under the compositor lock. A thread-local light
registry makes lights created on one thread invisible to the other.

Keep weak light registrations on ServerCompositor and use the owning
compositor for scene-lighting brushes, targeted light maps and moved
coordinate-space invalidation.

Add cross-thread regressions for XAML scene lights and explicitly targeted
composition lights. The scene-light regression fails before this fix.
All 97 composition tests pass after the change.
---
